<statement>
<p>Determine if the relation in each table is linear, exponential, or quadratic.</p>
<tabular>     <row><cell><em><m>\displaystyle{x}</m></em></cell><cell>0</cell><cell>1</cell><cell>2</cell><cell>3</cell><cell>4</cell><cell>5</cell></row>
<row><cell><em><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></em></cell><cell>5</cell><cell>8</cell><cell>11</cell><cell>14</cell><cell>17</cell><cell>20</cell></row>
</tabular><p>
 is: </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>Linear</li> 
<li>Exponential</li> 
<li>Quadratic</li> 
</ol></p>
<tabular>     <row><cell><em><m>\displaystyle{x}</m></em></cell><cell>0</cell><cell>1</cell><cell>2</cell><cell>3</cell><cell>4</cell><cell>5</cell></row>
<row><cell><em><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></em></cell><cell>5</cell><cell>10</cell><cell>20</cell><cell>40</cell><cell>80</cell><cell>160</cell></row>
</tabular><p>
 is: </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>Linear</li> 
<li>Exponential</li> 
<li>Quadratic</li> 
</ol></p>
<tabular>     <row><cell><em><m>\displaystyle{x}</m></em></cell><cell>0</cell><cell>1</cell><cell>2</cell><cell>3</cell><cell>4</cell><cell>5</cell></row>
<row><cell><em><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></em></cell><cell>4</cell><cell>5</cell><cell>7</cell><cell>10</cell><cell>14</cell><cell>19</cell></row>
</tabular><p>
 is: </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>Linear</li> 
<li>Exponential</li> 
<li>Quadratic</li> 
</ol></p>


</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>A: Linear</li><li>B: Exponential</li><li>C: Quadratic</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>The first one is Linear, because the differences are all 3.</p>
<p>The second one is Exponential, because the ratios are all 2.</p>
<p>The third on is Quadratic, because the second differences are all 1.</p></solution>
